  "sha1HashCodeDescription": "SHA-1 is a cryptographic hash algorithm that generates a 160-bit value. Today it is considered insecure for security use as it has known collisions. It is useful here only for educational purposes.",
  "sha256HashCodeTitle": "SHA-256",
  "sha256HashCodeDescription": "SHA-256 is a cryptographic hash algorithm from the SHA-2 family that generates a 256-bit value. It is widely used in security, blockchain, and secure data storage.",
